-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_59.sql (Isaiah 59) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 59 — SIN SEPARATES / NO INTERCESSOR / THE REDEEMER COMES TO ZION. The chapter
-- opens insisting the fault is not divine weakness: *Behold, the LORD'S hand is not shortened, that
-- it cannot save... But your iniquities have separated between you and your Elohim (God)* (59:1-2).
-- It rolls into the great depravity-catalogue (*their feet run to evil... The way of peace they know
-- not*, 59:3-8) — which Paul quotes VERBATIM in his universal-sin catena (Romans 3:15-17), answered
-- NOT by Torah-abolition but by Torah-establishing grace (*we establish the law*, Romans 3:31). The
-- people confess their darkness (59:9-15a), and then the hinge: *he saw that there was no man, and
-- wondered that there was no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation* (59:15b-16) — the
-- divine warrior, the arm of Yahuah revealed (Isaiah 53:1 / 52:10), the Formed Son, the sole
-- Redeemer, who *put on righteousness as a breastplate, and an helmet of salvation... clad with zeal
-- as a cloke* (59:17 -> the armour of Ephesians 6:14,17 + 1 Thess 5:8; the LORD's-zeal-as-armour
-- of Wisdom of Solomon 5:17-18). Then the keystone: *the Redeemer shall come to Zion, and unto them
-- that turn from transgression in Jacob* (59:20) — Paul quotes 59:20-21 in Romans 11:26-27 (*There
-- shall come out of Sion the Deliverer*), the two-house regathering, all Yashar'el saved (Rom 11:1-2
-- guard, NEVER replacement). And the everlasting covenant: *My spirit... and my words... shall not
-- depart out of thy mouth... for ever* (59:21) — Spirit + Word inseparable, the Torah on the heart
-- (Jeremiah 31:33), the Comforter abiding for ever (John 14:16-17).
