--      (★★ the everlasting covenant: Spirit + Word inseparable, never departing; the Torah on the heart, the Comforter abiding for ever)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★ THE HAND NOT SHORTENED (THREAD 1): *Behold, the LORD'S hand is not shortened, that it cannot
--      save; neither his ear heavy, that it cannot hear: But your iniquities have separated between you
--      and your Elohim (God), and your sins have hid his face from you* (59:1-2). The fault is never
--      divine weakness — it is sin that builds the barrier. Isaiah said it before of the put-away wife:
--      *Is my hand shortened at all, that it cannot redeem? or have I no power to deliver?* (Isaiah
--      50:2), and Yahuah said it to Moses over the quail: *Is the LORD'S hand waxed short?* (Numbers
--      11:23). The confession of vv.9-15a — *we wait for light, but behold obscurity... truth is fallen
--      in the street* — is that very separation worked out in the people's darkness; held in this thread
--      in prose, not forced to a separate add.
--   ★★ THE WAY OF PEACE THEY KNOW NOT (THREAD 2): the catalogue of sin — *your hands are defiled with
--      blood... Their feet run to evil, and they make haste to shed innocent blood... The way of peace
--      they know not* (59:3,7-8) — is the very text Paul stitches into his universal-depravity catena:
--      *Their feet are swift to shed blood: Destruction and misery are in their ways: And the way of
--      peace have they not known* (Romans 3:15-17), proving *they are all under sin* (3:9). But the
--      diagnosis is NOT answered by abolishing the Torah: *Do we then make void the law through faith?
--      Elohim (God) forbid: yea, we establish the law* (Romans 3:31). Victims-not-enemies — the CONDUCT
--      is condemned, the law upheld.
--   ★★★ NO INTERCESSOR — HIS OWN ARM (THREAD 3): *And Yahuah (LORD) saw it... And he saw that there was
--      no man, and wondered that there was no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation unto him;
--      and his righteousness, it sustained him. For he put on righteousness as a breastplate, and an
--      helmet of salvation upon his head... and was clad with zeal as a cloke* (59:15b-17). No man could
--      stand in the gap, so His own arm saves — the arm of Yahuah revealed (*to whom is the arm of
--      Yahuah (LORD) revealed?* Isaiah 53:1; *Yahuah (LORD) hath made bare his holy arm in the eyes of
--      all the nations* 52:10), the Formed Son, the sole Redeemer and sole intercessor: *one mediator
--      between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus)* (1 Timothy 2:5). And the
--      armour Yahuah Himself wore is the armour His people put on: *having on the breastplate of
--      righteousness... And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit* (Ephesians
--      6:14,17); *the breastplate of faith and love; and for an helmet, the hope of salvation* (1 Thess
--      5:8). The restored library witnesses the same picture: *He shall take to him his jealousy for
--      complete armour... He shall put on righteousness as a breastplate, and true judgment instead of
--      an helmet* (Wisdom of Solomon 5:17-18) — extras member, the LORD-clothed-in-His-own-zeal.
--   ★★★ THE REDEEMER SHALL COME TO ZION (THREAD 4): *So shall they fear the name of Yahuah (LORD) from
--      the west, and his glory from the rising of the sun... And the Redeemer shall come to Zion, and
--      unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob, saith Yahuah (LORD)* (59:19-20). Paul quotes
--      59:20-21 word for word as the seal of all-Israel's salvation: *And so all Yashar'el (Israel)
--      shall be saved: as it is written, There shall come out of Sion the Deliverer, and shall turn
--      away ungodliness from Jacob: For this is my covenant unto them, when I shall take away their
--      sins* (Romans 11:26-27). The Redeemer comes to Zion AND *unto them that turn from transgression*
--      — repentance, never antinomian — the two-house regathering: *He that scattered Yashar'el
--      (Israel) will gather him* (Jeremiah 31:10), under the guard that Elohim has NOT cast off His
--      people: *Hath Elohim (God) cast away his people? Elohim (God) forbid* (Romans 11:1). Never
--      replacement.
--   ★★ MY SPIRIT AND MY WORDS (THREAD 5): *As for me, this is my covenant with them, saith Yahuah
--      (LORD); My spirit that is upon thee, and my words which I have put in thy mouth, shall not depart
--      out of thy mouth, nor out of the mouth of thy seed... from henceforth and for ever* (59:21). The
--      everlasting covenant is Spirit AND Word together, never to depart — the same new covenant of the
--      Torah written within: *I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts*
--      (Jeremiah 31:33). And Yahusha promises the Spirit-with-the-Word abiding for ever: *he shall give
--      you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever; Even the Spirit of truth... he
--      dwelleth with you, and shall be in you* (John 14:16-17). Spirit and Word are inseparable; the
--      Torah is not abolished but interiorized and kept by the Spirit, for ever.
--   VERSES WITH NO SEPARATE ADD: v.9-15a (the confession of darkness — bound into THREAD 1 as the
--      separation of v.2 worked out, held in prose), v.18-19a (the recompence to adversaries and the
--      fear of the Name from west to east — the preface to the Redeemer-to-Zion of THREAD 4, woven in).
--      All recorded, none silently skipped. Extras: weighed 1 Enoch on the divine-warrior/Elect-One
--      judgment (skipped — the strong clean verbatim is Wisdom of Solomon 5:17-18, taken into THREAD 3;
--      avoided the known-bad 1 Enoch ch25 and the 62:5 apparatus).

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa59_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1 (★): Your iniquities have separated — the hand is not shortened
    ('canon','isaiah',59,1,'canon','isaiah',50,2,'free',
      E'*Wherefore, when I came, was there no man? when I called, was there none to answer? Is my hand shortened at all, that it cannot redeem? or have I no power to deliver?* (Isaiah 50:2). The same insistence opens this chapter — *Behold, the LORD''S hand is not shortened, that it cannot save* (Isaiah 59:1). The power to deliver was never lacking; in chapter 50 the mother was put away *for your iniquities*, and here too the barrier is sin, not a short hand.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,1,'canon','numbers',11,23,'free',
      E'*And Yahuah (LORD) said unto Moses, Is the LORD''S hand waxed short? thou shalt see now whether my word shall come to pass unto thee or not* (Numbers 11:23). When Moses doubted Yahuah could feed the multitude, the answer was the very phrase Isaiah takes up — *Behold, the LORD''S hand is not shortened, that it cannot save* (Isaiah 59:1). The hand that filled the wilderness with flesh is the hand that can always save; the want is never in Yahuah''s power.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,2,'canon','isaiah',50,1,'free',
      E'*Thus saith Yahuah (LORD), Where is the bill of your mother''s divorcement, whom I have put away?... Behold, for your iniquities have ye sold yourselves, and for your transgressions is your mother put away* (Isaiah 50:1). *But your iniquities have separated between you and your Elohim (God), and your sins have hid his face from you* (Isaiah 59:2) names the same cause: the separation, the hidden face, the put-away — all the fruit of iniquity, never of a failing on Yahuah''s part.'),

    -- THREAD 2 (★★): The way of peace they know not — Paul's depravity-catena quotes 59:7-8 verbatim
    ('canon','isaiah',59,7,'canon','romans',3,15,'free',
      E'*Their feet are swift to shed blood* (Romans 3:15). Paul lifts this straight from Isaiah — *Their feet run to evil, and they make haste to shed innocent blood* (Isaiah 59:7) — into his catena proving *they are all under sin* (Romans 3:9). The prophet''s indictment of the covenant people becomes Paul''s indictment of all flesh: the feet that run to evil.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,7,'canon','romans',3,16,'free',
      E'*Destruction and misery are in their ways* (Romans 3:16). This continues the verbatim quotation of Isaiah — *wasting and destruction are in their paths* (Isaiah 59:7). The thoughts of iniquity and the paths of wasting that Isaiah lays at the feet of the people, Paul gathers as the universal diagnosis of sin.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,8,'canon','romans',3,17,'free',
      E'*And the way of peace have they not known* (Romans 3:17). Word for word from Isaiah — *The way of peace they know not; and there is no judgment in their goings* (Isaiah 59:8). The crooked paths where no man finds peace are the climax of Paul''s catena: none righteous, none seeking, the way of peace unknown.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,8,'canon','romans',3,31,'free',
      E'*Do we then make void the law through faith? Elohim (God) forbid: yea, we establish the law* (Romans 3:31). After quoting Isaiah''s sin-catalogue (Isaiah 59:7-8) to convict all flesh, Paul does NOT conclude that the Torah is abolished — *we establish the law*. The universal-sin diagnosis is answered by Torah-establishing grace, not Torah-abolition; the conduct of *the way of peace they know not* (Isaiah 59:8) is condemned, the law upheld.'),

    -- THREAD 3 (★★★): There was no intercessor — therefore his own arm; the armour
    ('canon','isaiah',59,16,'canon','isaiah',53,1,'free',
      E'*Who hath believed our report? and to whom is the arm of Yahuah (LORD) revealed?* (Isaiah 53:1). *And he saw that there was no man, and wondered that there was no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation unto him* (Isaiah 59:16) — the very *arm of Yahuah* that chapter 53 unveils as the suffering Servant. No man could intercede, so the arm of Yahuah, the Formed Son, becomes the salvation.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,16,'canon','isaiah',52,10,'free',
      E'*Yahuah (LORD) hath made bare his holy arm in the eyes of all the nations; and all the ends of the earth shall see the salvation of our Elohim (God)* (Isaiah 52:10). When *there was no man, and... no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation* (Isaiah 59:16), it is this bared holy arm — Yahuah''s own saving arm, the Formed Son revealed to all nations, the sole Redeemer none other could supply.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,16,'canon','1-timothy',2,5,'free',
      E'*For there is one Elohim (God), and one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus)* (1 Timothy 2:5). Isaiah''s wonder that *there was no man... no intercessor* (Isaiah 59:16) is answered in the one Mediator — the MAN, the Formed Son who alone stands in the gap. No other intercessor was found; the arm of Yahuah itself became the one Mediator.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,17,'canon','ephesians',6,14,'free',
      E'*Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness* (Ephesians 6:14). *For he put on righteousness as a breastplate* (Isaiah 59:17) — the armour Yahuah Himself wore against the godless is the armour His people now put on. The breastplate of righteousness is His before it is ours; the warrior''s armour becomes the believer''s.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,17,'canon','ephesians',6,17,'free',
      E'*And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of Elohim (God)* (Ephesians 6:17). *And an helmet of salvation upon his head* (Isaiah 59:17) — the very helmet of the divine warrior is handed to the saints. The salvation Yahuah''s own arm brought (Isaiah 59:16) is worn as a helmet by the people He saves.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,17,'canon','1-thessalonians',5,8,'free',
      E'*But let us, who are of the day, be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love; and for an helmet, the hope of salvation* (1 Thessalonians 5:8). The same breastplate-and-helmet of the warrior of Isaiah 59:17 — *righteousness as a breastplate, and an helmet of salvation* — is what the children of the day put on. The armour Yahuah wore is the armour of those who wait for His day.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,17,'apocrypha','the-wisdom-of-solomon',5,17,'extras',
      E'*He shall take to him his jealousy for complete armour, and make the creature his weapon for the revenge of his enemies* (Wisdom of Solomon 5:17). This is the same picture as *and was clad with zeal as a cloke* (Isaiah 59:17) — Yahuah arming Himself with His own jealousy/zeal to repay His adversaries. The restored library witnesses the divine warrior clothing Himself in zeal to bring judgment and salvation.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,17,'apocrypha','the-wisdom-of-solomon',5,18,'extras',
      E'*He shall put on righteousness as a breastplate, and true judgment instead of an helmet* (Wisdom of Solomon 5:18). Almost word for word with *he put on righteousness as a breastplate, and an helmet of salvation upon his head* (Isaiah 59:17). The whole armour of the LORD — breastplate of righteousness, helmet — is sung twice in the library, the warrior who saves by His own arm when no man is found.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★★★): The Redeemer shall come to Zion — Paul quotes 59:20-21 in Romans 11
    ('canon','isaiah',59,20,'canon','romans',11,26,'free',
      E'*And so all Yashar''el (Israel) shall be saved: as it is written, There shall come out of Sion the Deliverer, and shall turn away ungodliness from Jacob* (Romans 11:26). Paul quotes Isaiah word for word — *And the Redeemer shall come to Zion, and unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob, saith Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 59:20). The Redeemer to Zion IS the seal of all-Israel''s salvation: the Deliverer comes, and ungodliness is turned away from Jacob.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,21,'canon','romans',11,27,'free',
      E'*For this is my covenant unto them, when I shall take away their sins* (Romans 11:27). Paul continues quoting Isaiah — *As for me, this is my covenant with them, saith Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 59:21). The covenant attached to the Redeemer-come-to-Zion is the covenant that takes away sins; the turning from transgression of Isaiah 59:20 is the sins taken away of Romans 11:27.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,20,'canon','romans',11,1,'free',
      E'*I say then, Hath Elohim (God) cast away his people? Elohim (God) forbid. For I also am an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham* (Romans 11:1). The Redeemer coming *to Zion, and unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob* (Isaiah 59:20) is no replacement of the people — *Elohim (God) hath not cast away his people which he foreknew* (Romans 11:2). The same Jacob whose transgression is turned away is the people gathered, never cast off.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,20,'canon','jeremiah',31,10,'free',
      E'*Hear the word of Yahuah (LORD), O ye nations... He that scattered Yashar''el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* (Jeremiah 31:10). *The Redeemer shall come to Zion, and unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob* (Isaiah 59:20) is that very gathering — the scattered houses brought home to the One who scattered and now gathers, the two-house regathering of them that turn (repent), never a new people grafted in by confession.'),

    -- THREAD 5 (★★): My spirit and my words shall not depart — the everlasting covenant
    ('canon','isaiah',59,21,'canon','jeremiah',31,33,'free',
      E'*But this shall be the covenant that I will make with the house of Yashar''el (Israel)... I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts; and will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people* (Jeremiah 31:33). *My spirit that is upon thee, and my words which I have put in thy mouth, shall not depart* (Isaiah 59:21) is the same everlasting covenant — Spirit AND Word together, the Torah written within and never to depart. The covenant is not the law abolished but the law interiorized.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,21,'canon','john',14,16,'free',
      E'*And I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever* (John 14:16). *My spirit that is upon thee... shall not depart out of thy mouth... from henceforth and for ever* (Isaiah 59:21) — the abiding Spirit Yahusha promises is the Spirit-of-the-covenant that does not depart. The Comforter who abides *for ever* is the everlasting Spirit upon the seed and the seed''s seed.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',59,21,'canon','john',14,17,'free',
      E'*Even the Spirit of truth; whom the world cannot receive... for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you* (John 14:17). The covenant of *my spirit that is upon thee, and my words* (Isaiah 59:21) is Spirit and Word inseparable — the Spirit of truth indwelling, the words never departing. The Spirit dwells within and the words remain in the mouth; the covenant that Yahusha fulfils is the Spirit-and-Word together for ever.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa59_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa59_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-59-your-iniquities-have-separated-between-you-and-your-elohim',
       E'Your iniquities have separated — the hand is not shortened',
       E'The chapter opens by refusing the lie that Yahuah is the problem: *Behold, the LORD''S hand is not shortened, that it cannot save; neither his ear heavy, that it cannot hear: But your iniquities have separated between you and your Elohim (God), and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear* (Isaiah 59:1-2). The fault is sin, never divine weakness — the barrier is built by iniquity, the hidden face is earned. Isaiah had said the same over the put-away mother: *Is my hand shortened at all, that it cannot redeem? or have I no power to deliver?* (Isaiah 50:2); *for your iniquities have ye sold yourselves, and for your transgressions is your mother put away* (50:1). And Yahuah said it to Moses when the people doubted He could feed them: *Is the LORD''S hand waxed short?* (Numbers 11:23). The power to save was never lacking. The confession that follows — *Therefore is judgment far from us... we wait for light, but behold obscurity; for brightness, but we walk in darkness... truth is fallen in the street* (59:9,14) — is that separation worked out in the people''s own darkness: the groping, the stumbling at noonday, the desolate places, all the harvest of the iniquity that separated them from their Elohim. The light is not withheld by a short hand; it is shut out by sin.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27450
  FROM _s303_isa59_lookup sv, _s303_isa59_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=59 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=59 AND ev.verse_number=2
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-59-the-way-of-peace-they-know-not',
       E'The way of peace they know not — Paul''s catena, and the law established',
       E'The separation of verse 2 is unfolded in a catalogue of sin: *For your hands are defiled with blood... your lips have spoken lies... Their feet run to evil, and they make haste to shed innocent blood: their thoughts are thoughts of iniquity; wasting and destruction are in their paths. The way of peace they know not; and there is no judgment in their goings* (Isaiah 59:3,7-8). Paul takes these very lines into his great catena proving *they are all under sin* (Romans 3:9): *Their feet are swift to shed blood: Destruction and misery are in their ways: And the way of peace have they not known* (Romans 3:15-17) — word for word from Isaiah 59:7-8. The prophet''s indictment of the covenant people becomes Paul''s universal diagnosis of all flesh. But mark how Paul ENDS the argument: not by discarding the Torah, but by upholding it — *Do we then make void the law through faith? Elohim (God) forbid: yea, we establish the law* (Romans 3:31). The depravity-diagnosis is answered by Torah-establishing grace, never Torah-abolition. The conduct is condemned — the bloody hands, the lying lips, the feet swift to evil — and the law that condemns it stands. Victims, not enemies: the systems of iniquity are dismantled; the instruction of Yahuah is established.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27453
  FROM _s303_isa59_lookup sv, _s303_isa59_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=59 AND sv.verse_number=3
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=59 AND ev.verse_number=8
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-59-there-was-no-intercessor-therefore-his-own-arm',
       E'There was no man, no intercessor — therefore His own arm, clad with zeal',
       E'Here is the hinge of the chapter: *And Yahuah (LORD) saw it, and it displeased him that there was no judgment. And he saw that there was no man, and wondered that there was no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation unto him; and his righteousness, it sustained him. For he put on righteousness as a breastplate, and an helmet of salvation upon his head; and he put on the garments of vengeance for clothing, and was clad with zeal as a cloke* (Isaiah 59:15b-17). No man could stand in the gap, no intercessor was found — so Yahuah''s OWN arm saves. That arm is no abstraction: it is *the arm of Yahuah (LORD)* that Isaiah 53:1 unveils as the suffering Servant — *to whom is the arm of Yahuah (LORD) revealed?* — and the *holy arm* Yahuah *made bare in the eyes of all the nations* (Isaiah 52:10). The arm is the Formed Son, the sole Redeemer, *one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus)* (1 Timothy 2:5) — the one intercessor when none other could be found. And the armour the divine warrior wore is the armour His people now put on: *having on the breastplate of righteousness... And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of Elohim (God)* (Ephesians 6:14,17); *the breastplate of faith and love; and for an helmet, the hope of salvation* (1 Thessalonians 5:8). The restored library sings the same warrior twice over: *He shall take to him his jealousy for complete armour... He shall put on righteousness as a breastplate, and true judgment instead of an helmet* (Wisdom of Solomon 5:17-18) — Yahuah clothing Himself in His own zeal to repay His adversaries and bring salvation by His own arm.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 27456
  FROM _s303_isa59_lookup sv, _s303_isa59_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=59 AND sv.verse_number=15
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=59 AND ev.verse_number=17
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-59-the-redeemer-shall-come-to-zion',
       E'The Redeemer shall come to Zion — all Yashar''el saved, them that turn from transgression',
       E'The chapter rises from sin and salvation to the great promise: *So shall they fear the name of Yahuah (LORD) from the west, and his glory from the rising of the sun... And the Redeemer shall come to Zion, and unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob, saith Yahuah (LORD). As for me, this is my covenant with them, saith Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 59:19-21). Paul quotes Isaiah 59:20-21 word for word as the very seal of all-Israel''s salvation: *And so all Yashar''el (Israel) shall be saved: as it is written, There shall come out of Sion the Deliverer, and shall turn away ungodliness from Jacob: For this is my covenant unto them, when I shall take away their sins* (Romans 11:26-27). Note carefully WHO the Redeemer comes to: *unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob* — repentance, the turning away of ungodliness, never an antinomian welcome. And note the guard Paul sets around the whole passage: *Hath Elohim (God) cast away his people? Elohim (God) forbid... Elohim (God) hath not cast away his people which he foreknew* (Romans 11:1-2). This is no replacement of Israel by another people; it is the two-house regathering — *He that scattered Yashar''el (Israel) will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock* (Jeremiah 31:10). The Redeemer comes to Zion, the fear of the Name spreads from west to the rising sun, and the scattered, repentant houses of Jacob are gathered home and their sins taken away.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27459
  FROM _s303_isa59_lookup sv, _s303_isa59_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=59 AND sv.verse_number=18
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=59 AND ev.verse_number=20
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 5 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-59-my-spirit-and-my-words-shall-not-depart-for-ever',
       E'My spirit and my words shall not depart — the everlasting covenant within',
       E'The chapter closes on the everlasting covenant: *As for me, this is my covenant with them, saith Yahuah (LORD); My spirit that is upon thee, and my words which I have put in thy mouth, shall not depart out of thy mouth, nor out of the mouth of thy seed, nor out of the mouth of thy seed''s seed, saith Yahuah (LORD), from henceforth and for ever* (Isaiah 59:21). The covenant is Spirit AND Word together — never the one without the other, never to depart, carried down the generations of the seed for ever. This is the same new covenant Jeremiah names: *I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts; and will be their Elohim (God), and they shall be my people* (Jeremiah 31:33) — the Torah not abolished but written within, the words in the mouth and on the heart. And Yahusha promises the abiding Spirit who carries that Word: *I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you for ever; Even the Spirit of truth... for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you* (John 14:16-17). The Spirit indwells, the words remain — inseparable. The everlasting covenant of Isaiah 59:21 is the Spirit-and-Word interiorized, the Torah on the heart kept by the Spirit of truth, from henceforth and for ever.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27462
  FROM _s303_isa59_lookup sv, _s303_isa59_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=59 AND sv.verse_number=21
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=59 AND ev.verse_number=21
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

